  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\n\nA channel of sfc high pressure moves through the area on \nThanksgiving Day resulting in little to no cloud cover and highs in \nthe 40s.\n\nAnother H5 impulse will eject from British Columbia/Alberta and \ntrack east southeast toward the Northern Plains late Friday. Ahead \nof the feature, we'll see ridging resulting in warming temperatures \nup to the 50s. As the wave arrives at our doorstep, increasing mid \nlevel forcing for ascent and height falls coupled with a stream of \nPacific moisture will lead to a small chance for rain Saturday \n(15- 20%), although there is some spread observed amongst model \nsolutions regarding the placement of the wave and how fast it \nejects. Significant model spread is observed through Monday with\nvarious members suggesting flow aloft remaining zonal to \nnorthwesterly. Highs this weekend through Monday remain in the \n40s and 50s.",
